// Title: Windows Defender Service Disabled - Registry
// Sigma ID: e1aa95de-610a-427d-b9e7-9b46cfafbe6a
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Ján Trenčanský, frack113, AlertIQ, Nasreddine Bencherchali
// Date: 2022-08-01 | Modified: 2024-03-25
// ATT&CK: defense-impairment, T1685
// Description: Detects when an attacker or tool disables the Windows Defender service (WinDefend) via the
//   registry
// False positives:
//   - Administrator actions
// References:
//   - https://thedfirreport.com/2021/10/18/icedid-to-xinglocker-ransomware-in-24-hours/
//   - https://gist.github.com/anadr/7465a9fde63d41341136949f14c21105
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_disable_windows_defender_service.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where RegistryKey endswith "\\Services\\WinDefend\\Start" and RegistryValueData =~ "DWORD (0x00000004)"
